<ExerciseBridge title="Next up:" size="wide">

# Links and Anchors

Links connect sources and places within a page. The `<a>` element turns part of your content into a hyperlink readers can follow.

</ExerciseBridge>

<ExerciseBridge title="Why Anchor?" size="wide">

The term **anchor** specifically refers to the `<a>` element's ability to mark a precise location in a webpage that can be jumped to, like bookmarking a spot within the same document. This is related with the `#`-fragment as part of the URL in an earlier exercise.

Learn more about anchors and fragments in the [MDN Leraning Center](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Structuring_content/Creating_links#document_fragments), since you will use this in the *Mini project*.

</ExerciseBridge>

<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('nesting-anchors')} />

