<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('link-title-accessibility')} />

<ExerciseBridge title="Anchors vs. Buttons" size="wide">

There is an important distinction to make between anchors (`<a>`) and buttons (`<button>`): Anchors should be used for *navigation* whereas buttons are intended for *actions*, like e.g. opening an accordion or submitting a form.

Unfortunately, buttons are often misused as anchors, and it's important to know this distinction early. Later, when you will learn Svelte or javascript it's very tempting to use a button for navigation, like so: 

```html
<button onclick={goto("/foo/bar")}>
```

**This is problematic,** since a button does not carry the same semantic meaning. Accordingly, this misuse comes with major accessibility issues.

</ExerciseBridge>

<ExerciseCard question={getQuestion('buttons-vs-anchors')} />

